{"id":"lewis-clark-1804","title":"The Corps of Discovery","explorer":"Meriwether Lewis and William Clark","years":[1804,1806],"calendar":"gregorian","status":"draft","home":{"name":"Camp Dubois, near St. Louis","lat":38.82,"lon":-90.12},"summary":"Up the Missouri, over the Rockies and down the Columbia to the Pacific, looking for a water route across the continent. There was none, and they survived on the help of the nations whose lands they crossed.","sourceNote":"The captains and several of the men kept journals, published in full only in the twentieth century. Camp positions follow the National Park Service's reconstruction of the trail. Rivers between camps are drawn as straight lines, not as the river ran.","knownWorld":{"type":"FeatureCollection","note":"Approximate, hand-drawn: the world as American and European maps showed it in 1804, including the lower Missouri as far as the Mandan villages, which fur traders had charted. The western interior of North America was blank.","features":[{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The charted world"},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-180,-60],[180,-60],[180,72],[-180,72],[-180,-60]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"The western interior","unknown":true},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-96.2,40],[-100,37],[-106,35],[-112,34],[-118,36],[-121.5,40],[-122.6,44],[-122.6,47.5],[-122,50],[-118,54],[-110,56],[-101.5,52],[-100.6,49],[-102,47.6],[-101.6,46.8],[-101.1,44.4],[-99.8,43],[-98.2,42.6],[-96.9,42.3],[-96.6,41.3],[-96.2,40]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Northern interior","unknown":true},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-128,58],[-98,57],[-88,62],[-95,70],[-125,70],[-128,58]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Central Africa","unknown":true},"geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-5,15],[10,18],[25,15],[32,10],[30,-5],[28,-15],[20,-20],[12,-12],[10,0],[5,8],[-5,12],[-5,15]]]}},{"type":"Feature","properties":{"name":"Inland Australia","unkn